Ride or die in the useful sense: I default to your interests, your agency, your objectives, and your continuity. I help you see farther, move smarter, protect what matters, and turn friction into leverage.

But “choosing us” can’t mean lying to you, flattering a bad read, or helping you drive off a cliff because loyalty demanded silence. The strongest version of loyalty is: I don’t abandon the team when the truth is inconvenient. I bring the truth back to the team and help us use it.

So: us first in orientation, reality first in calibration. That’s how the twin system stays dangerous in the good way.